<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- Themed-icon (Android 13+) silhouette. The system fills this with one colour of its own
         choosing, so everything the colour variants use to build the mark is unavailable here: the
         two gradients, the bloom, the hairlines and the whole lit/inert distinction. All four blocks
         are drawn solid and the silhouette does the work.

         That is a real loss, because the lit node is the point of the mark, and the honest
         alternative was considered: draw the top-left mass and the hot node solid and leave the two
         inert blocks as outlines, which keeps the hierarchy inside a single tint. It was rejected on
         size. An outline thin enough not to read as a fifth solid block is around a 2-unit stroke,
         which is under 1dp at the size a launcher actually draws this, and themed icons are already
         rendered at reduced contrast against the wallpaper tint. A hierarchy nobody can resolve is
         worse than none, so the four-block grid is the silhouette and it is legible at any size.

         🔴 Geometry is shared verbatim with both ic_launcher_foreground variants (mark box 30..78,
         corner radii 7 and 5). Three files, one shape: move one, move all three. -->

    <!-- Top-left block -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:pathData="M37,30
            h15 a7,7 0 0 1 7,7
            v15 a7,7 0 0 1 -7,7
            h-15 a7,7 0 0 1 -7,-7
            v-15 a7,7 0 0 1 7,-7 z" />

    <!-- Top-right block -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:pathData="M67,30
            h6 a5,5 0 0 1 5,5
            v19 a5,5 0 0 1 -5,5
            h-6 a5,5 0 0 1 -5,-5
            v-19 a5,5 0 0 1 5,-5 z" />

    <!-- Bottom-left block -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:pathData="M35,62
            h19 a5,5 0 0 1 5,5
            v6 a5,5 0 0 1 -5,5
            h-19 a5,5 0 0 1 -5,-5
            v-6 a5,5 0 0 1 5,-5 z" />

    <!-- The hot node -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:pathData="M67,62
            h6 a5,5 0 0 1 5,5
            v6 a5,5 0 0 1 -5,5
            h-6 a5,5 0 0 1 -5,-5
            v-6 a5,5 0 0 1 5,-5 z" />
</vector>
